{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02843",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 7.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "Doctor, this one's ready for you. Everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.21,
      "end_seconds": 12.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.32,
      "end_seconds": 21.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "Oh, um, hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.32,
      "end_seconds": 25.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.56,
      "end_seconds": 40.49,
      "duration_seconds": 12.93,
      "text": "Well, I've been having a rolled ankle. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.09,
      "end_seconds": 45.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.08,
      "end_seconds": 59.79,
      "duration_seconds": 10.71,
      "text": "Levetiracetam. I take it 500 milligrams, twice a day. Clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, maybe, once a day for the stent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.43,
      "end_seconds": 65.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.56,
      "end_seconds": 76.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so no, it's at home. Ibuprofen gel, three times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.61,
      "end_seconds": 81.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.07,
      "end_seconds": 87.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "About about a month, give or take."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 87.64,
      "end_seconds": 91.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "It was closer to about two months, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.2,
      "end_seconds": 100.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.57,
      "end_seconds": 105.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "I mean, that sounds about right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.84,
      "end_seconds": 112.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "Mm, I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 112.53,
      "end_seconds": 119.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.71,
      "end_seconds": 122.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.71,
      "end_seconds": 128.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "Oh, and some swelling. That's been about the same, about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.85,
      "end_seconds": 133.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.14,
      "end_seconds": 142.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "Well, you know, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.84,
      "end_seconds": 149.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Okay, take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.4,
      "end_seconds": 154.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "About a five out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 155.17,
      "end_seconds": 157.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Yes, exactly like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.4,
      "end_seconds": 169.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "And pain in the shin, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.09,
      "end_seconds": 174.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, no pain in the shin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.94,
      "end_seconds": 181.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Any numbness, pop or pain in the foot at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.84,
      "end_seconds": 195.42,
      "duration_seconds": 12.58,
      "text": "No, no numbness, no pop, no pain in the foot. I did have bruising at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.44,
      "end_seconds": 203.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.78,
      "end_seconds": 206.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "No weakness or anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.18,
      "end_seconds": 210.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.38,
      "end_seconds": 214.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.81,
      "end_seconds": 218.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.79,
      "end_seconds": 225.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Just a wisdom tooth extraction under sedation, five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.88,
      "end_seconds": 228.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.51,
      "end_seconds": 233.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.27,
      "end_seconds": 237.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.71,
      "end_seconds": 242.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.68,
      "end_seconds": 248.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.1,
      "end_seconds": 260.4,
      "duration_seconds": 10.3,
      "text": "So, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.2,
      "end_seconds": 263.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.5,
      "end_seconds": 267.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "I've got epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.08,
      "end_seconds": 268.99,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.74,
      "end_seconds": 273.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Well, I've had heart disease, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.24,
      "end_seconds": 285.69,
      "duration_seconds": 10.45,
      "text": "Sure. Yes, epilepsy and heart disease are known to us, good to have that clear. Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.42,
      "end_seconds": 291.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Okay, um, so my daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 304.17,
      "end_seconds": 314.01,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Oxygen saturation is 98 percent, BP is 120 over 76, respiratory rate 18. Temp 36.8 degrees, pulse 83."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.89,
      "end_seconds": 317.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.94,
      "end_seconds": 321.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.54,
      "end_seconds": 324.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.18,
      "end_seconds": 348.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "There is mild swelling over the outer ankle but no bony tenderness and you can take four steps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.74,
      "end_seconds": 374.14,
      "duration_seconds": 21.4,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Okay, thinking it through, I'd lean towards a mild ankle sprain. Rest, ice, compression and elevation, then gradual strengthening. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.06,
      "end_seconds": 379.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.63,
      "end_seconds": 395.77,
      "duration_seconds": 15.14,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. I'll want another look if not better in two weeks. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.31,
      "end_seconds": 398.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Well, thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.06,
      "end_seconds": 401.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}